  "code": "use IO.Std.write_line;\nuse Collections.LIST;\n\nlet squares = LIST[() -> int]();\n\n// The loop variable is immutable and scoped to the loop body, so every iteration has its own. An\n// immutable local is captured by value, so each function holds the number its own iteration had.\nfor i in 0..10 do\n    squares.add(() => i * i);\nod\n\nwrite_line(\"{squares[3]()}\");",
